{"title":"1999 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video(By_YippieMath)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video(By YippieMath)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the degree measure of the smaller angle formed by the hands of a clock at 10 o'clock?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/4500534f275d08449e027ed4322baa4c284ea69e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw(circle((0,0),2)); dot((0,0)); for(int i = 0; i &lt; 12; ++i) { dot(2*dir(30*i)); }  label(&quot;$3$&quot;,2*dir(0),W); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,2*dir(30),WSW); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,2*dir(60),SSW); label(&quot;$12$&quot;,2*dir(90),S); label(&quot;$11$&quot;,2*dir(120),SSE); label(&quot;$10$&quot;,2*dir(150),ESE); label(&quot;$9$&quot;,2*dir(180),E); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,2*dir(210),ENE); label(&quot;$7$&quot;,2*dir(240),NNE); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,2*dir(270),N); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,2*dir(300),NNW); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,2*dir(330),WNW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c846b46e05b7d17d3e1c0fac76b96bc5eb5f2c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 45 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 60 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 75 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f47b8281adebaee3df2478a9229035d042e7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10:00$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, the hour hand will be on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> while the minute hand on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>This makes them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />th of a circle apart, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/a/0ea158e1a28ebce9036015a69a21032af641a1f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot360^{\\circ}=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"152\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the full clock is a circle, and therefore has 360 degrees. Considering that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, the distance between one number will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c47c8a43be25e5fd15af6e2078511ad209dd89f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$360\\div 12=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />.\nIf the time is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f47b8281adebaee3df2478a9229035d042e7ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10:00$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"13\" />, then the hour hand will be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and the minute hand will be on, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, making them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers apart, so they will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> degrees apart, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe281610de938d7642af35722c5b657368dd2b23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } 60}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video.28By_YippieMath.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video(By_YippieMath)\">Video(By YippieMath)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video(By YippieMath)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qop08mDP6HY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qop08mDP6HY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8\" title=\"1999 AMC 8\">1999 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td wi